KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ member insert\(\{a,b\}\) constructs the class parameter: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [over.match.list], [dcl.init.list]/3: a braced-init-list argument to a
member function whose parameter is a class type must be copy-list-initialized
(the parameter type's constructors considered with the list elements).  CBMC's
member-call overload resolution does not do this (free-function calls do), so
`m.insert({a,b})` reports "found no match for symbol 'insert'".  Root of the
dominant insert-noise cluster in the src/util dog-food (found by cvise).  Flip
to CORE once member calls accept braced-init-list arguments for class params.
